Cell["Reading files and building the grid/derivatives", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.972037821001741*^9, 
  3.972037844844709*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0cea8585-afc8-44c9-930d-\
515c6ded166d"],

Cell["\<\
Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s define the initial number step, the final one, and the \
interval between each step that is going to be imported.
Foldername contains the location of the output file in your laptop.
For TypeOfFile, you can choose \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]constrained\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]bulk\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]boundary\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] depending which kind of \
file you want to read (and which one you have in the folder!).\
\>", "Text",
