Cell["\<\
I use the values of Fy, Fx and A at the boundary. In my case this correspond \
to the index 6, 5 and -2 (they vary depending on which type of quantity you \
are analysing, and on the number of u-subdomains).
For getting the velocities, I am using the expression coming from  \
https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.00032.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.972038279413241*^9, 3.972038302241507*^9}, {
  3.9720383594261713`*^9, 3.9720383648117037`*^9}, {3.9720384880147963`*^9, 
